@node dokgen_assets
@section (dokgen assets)

@c %start of fragment

A Texinfo chapter is complete without these two files, and Info and
print output never see them.  They are what makes the HTML a reader
expects from reference documentation: the definition as a card with its
signature at the top, an index of those definitions down the side with a
filter, a button that copies a signature, a folded tail on the long
ones, a theme that follows the reader, and diagrams that open into
something they can zoom into and drag.

They are written into the destination beside the chapter, so a manual
that is built with this directory on its include path and these two
files beside its pages gets all of it, and a manual that ignores them
gets a chapter that still reads.  The JavaScript is progressive and has
no dependencies: every feature is one selector away from disappearing.

The manual of this project says how a build points at them; `maak
manual' does it.


@c %end of fragment

