@node dokgen_commands
@section (dokgen commands)

@c %start of fragment

This module defines procedures that are associated to every command
provided by the command-line interface of the @command{dokgen} program.
See the @ref{CLI} and @xref{dokgen_cli,(dokgen cli)} sections for
additional information.

The variable @code{DEFAULT_DOC_PATH} is the directory where the API
documentation is saved when the user does not choose one; its value is
@samp{doc/api}.  The documentation is written to a file named
@file{index.texi} inside that directory, and the images of the mermaid
diagrams it holds go in a @file{diagrams} directory beside it.

The procedure @code{api} writes that documentation; @code{check} only
reads, and says which of the exported names are documented nowhere.

@image{diagrams/dokgen_commands-cec3eac2,,,Mermaid diagram}


@c %end of fragment

@c %start of fragment

@subsection Overview
@itemize 
@item
@ref{dokgen_commands_api,api} — Extract the API documentation of the given set of Guile Scheme


@item
@ref{dokgen_commands_check,check} — Report the exported names the modules in SOURCES leave undocumented.


@item
@ref{dokgen_commands_stats,stats} — Measure the tree SOURCES hold and write its statistics chapter.


@item
@ref{dokgen_commands_DEFAULT_DOC_PATH,DEFAULT_DOC_PATH} — A variable.


@end itemize


@c %end of fragment

@c %start of fragment

@subsection Procedures

@c %start of fragment

@anchor{dokgen_commands_api}
@deffn Procedure api sources OPT: destination mermaid-command
Extract the API documentation of the given set of Guile Scheme modules.

@strong{sources} (list of strings): Absolute or relative paths to Guile
Scheme modules that compose the code whose API documentation will be
extracted.  These paths can lead to both Scheme files or Scheme
directories.  For example:

@example 
(list «myproject/liby.scm»
      «myproject/liby»
      «myproject/libz.scm»
      «myproject/libz»)
@end example

@strong{destination} (string): Optional path to a directory where the
final Texinfo files will be saved.  If not provided,
@var{DEFAULT_DOC_PATH} is used (see the module @ref{dokgen_commands}).
The diagrams the documentation holds are saved to a @file{diagrams}
directory inside it.

@strong{mermaid-command} (string): Optional command that draws a mermaid
diagram, with @code{%i} standing for the diagram's source and @code{%o}
for the path to write its image to.  An empty command draws nothing and
uses the diagrams already in the destination.

@strong{Result}: The API documentation is saved to the @var{destination}
directory.

@end deffn


@c %end of fragment

@c %start of fragment

@anchor{dokgen_commands_check}
@deffn Procedure check sources
Report the exported names the modules in SOURCES leave undocumented.

@strong{sources} (list of strings): Absolute or relative paths to Scheme
files and directories, as for @code{api}.

@strong{Return value} (integer): The number of names reported, so that
the caller decides what an undocumented name means for the exit status.

@end deffn


@c %end of fragment

@c %start of fragment

@anchor{dokgen_commands_stats}
@deffn Procedure stats sources OPT: destination
Measure the tree SOURCES hold and write its statistics chapter.

@strong{sources} (list of strings): Absolute or relative paths to Scheme
files and directories, as for @code{api}.

@strong{destination} (string): Optional path to a directory where the
Texinfo chapter will be saved.  If not provided, @var{DEFAULT_DOC_PATH}
is used.  The chapter is named @file{stats.texi}, so that a manual can
include it beside the API chapter @code{api} writes.

@strong{Result}: The statistics are saved to the @var{destination}
directory, and the numbers a reader of a terminal wants are printed.

@end deffn


@c %end of fragment

@c %end of fragment

@c %start of fragment

@subsection Variables

@c %start of fragment

@anchor{dokgen_commands_DEFAULT_DOC_PATH}
@defvr Variable DEFAULT_DOC_PATH
@verbatim 
"doc/api"
@end verbatim

@end defvr


@c %end of fragment

@c %end of fragment

@c %end of fragment

@c %start of fragment

@node dokgen_data
@section (dokgen data)

@c %start of fragment

This module defines procedures to retrieve data from Guile Scheme
libraries (e.g.  the names and attributes of their Scheme modules and
the objects these modules export).  This data is then passed to template
procedures to render API documentation in different formats.  See, for
example, the templates used to work with the
@uref{https://www.gnu.org/software/texinfo/,Texinfo format}:
@ref{dokgen_templates_stexi,(dokgen templates stexi)}.


@c %end of fragment

@c %start of fragment

@subsection Overview
@itemize 
@item
@ref{dokgen_data_api-symbols,api-symbols} — Return the symbols provided by the interface.


@item
@ref{dokgen_data_file-path->module-name,file-path->module-name} — Convert the given Scheme file path into a module name.


@item
@ref{dokgen_data_get-file-paths,get-file-paths} — Return a list of paths to Scheme files stored in the directory.


@item
@ref{dokgen_data_group-api-objects,group-api-objects} — Return the API objects grouped by kind.


@item
@ref{dokgen_data_record-field,record-field} — Get the value of @var{field} from @var{record}.


@item
@ref{dokgen_data_undocumented-symbols,undocumented-symbols} — Return the names @var{interface} exports without documenting them.


@end itemize


@c %end of fragment

@c %start of fragment

@subsection Procedures

@c %start of fragment

@anchor{dokgen_data_api-symbols}
@deffn Procedure api-symbols interface
Return the symbols provided by the interface.

@strong{interface} (interface): A module's @code{<interface>} record as
returned by Guile's procedure @code{resolve-interface}.

@strong{Return value} (list of symbols): Where every symbol identifies a
public object exported by the @var{interface}.

@end deffn


@c %end of fragment

@c %start of fragment

@anchor{dokgen_data_file-path->module-name}
@deffn Procedure file-path->module-name file-path lib-parent-path
Convert the given Scheme file path into a module name.

@strong{file-path} (string): Absolute path to Guile Scheme module file.
For example: @samp{/home/user/project-x/libx/module-a.scm}.

@strong{lib-parent-path} (string): Absolute path to the directory
containing the library @var{file-path} belongs to.  For example:
@samp{/home/user/project-x/}.

@strong{Return value} (symbol): The name of the module.  For example:
@code{(libx module-a)}.

@end deffn


@c %end of fragment

@c %start of fragment

@anchor{dokgen_data_get-file-paths}
@deffn Procedure get-file-paths directory
Return a list of paths to Scheme files stored in the directory.

Scheme files are identified by their @code{.scm} extension.

@strong{directory} (string): Absolute path to a directory containing a
Guile Scheme library.

@strong{Return value} (list of strings): A list where every element
represents a path to a Scheme file.

@end deffn


@c %end of fragment

@c %start of fragment

@anchor{dokgen_data_group-api-objects}
@deffn Procedure group-api-objects interface
Return the API objects grouped by kind.

A kind can be one of the following: macros, parameters, procedures,
record types, variables.

@strong{interface} (interface): An @code{<interface>} record as returned
by Guile's procedure @code{resolve-interface}.

@strong{Return value} (alist): Association list where every entry
corresponds to a kind of object and a list of its members.  Only groups
with members are returned.

@end deffn


@c %end of fragment

@c %start of fragment

@anchor{dokgen_data_record-field}
@deffn Procedure record-field record field
Get the value of @var{field} from @var{record}.

@strong{record} (Guile record or SRFI 9 record): A record of any type.

@strong{field} (symbol): The name of the field.

@strong{Return value} (anything): The value of the field.

If the FIELD does not exist, a @var{no-such-field} exception is raised.

@end deffn


@c %end of fragment

@c %start of fragment

@anchor{dokgen_data_undocumented-symbols}
@deffn Procedure undocumented-symbols interface
Return the names @var{interface} exports without documenting them.

@strong{interface} (interface): A module's @code{<interface>} record, as
returned by Guile's procedure @code{resolve-interface}.

@strong{Return value} (list of symbols): The documented gaps of the
module's API, in the order a reader meets them in the manual, so that a
build can fail on them.  An export that is bound to nothing is left out:
that name is a bug in the module and not a gap in its documentation, and
the @code{api} command is where it is reported.

@end deffn


@c %end of fragment

@c %end of fragment

@c %end of fragment

@c %start of fragment

@node dokgen_diagrams
@section (dokgen diagrams)

@c %start of fragment

This module turns the mermaid diagrams a documentation string carries
into images the manual can show.

A diagram is written in a docstring as a fenced block, the way a
markdown reader already knows.  What follows is one, and it is drawn
where the manual shows this module:

@image{diagrams/dokgen_diagrams-bc388dc4,,,Mermaid diagram}

The fence is consumed, the diagram is written next to the generated
Texinfo as @file{diagrams/NAME-HASH.mmd}, and a renderer turns it into
@file{diagrams/NAME-HASH.png}, which the API chapter references with
@code{@@image}.  The name carries a digest of the diagram's own text, so
a diagram that changed gets a file of its own and an old rendering can
never be shown as the current one.

The renderer is a command, not a library: mermaid is JavaScript, and a
documentation generator that embedded a browser to draw an arrow would
be a worse trade than one that calls the tool a project already uses.
The command @code{mmdc} (from @code{mermaid-cli}) is the default; the
parameters @code{*mermaid-command*} and @code{*diagram-destination*} say
what to run and where to write, so a caller sets them once around a
whole run.  A command left empty renders nothing, which is how a tree
that commits its images builds its manual without a renderer.

When there is no image, the diagram's source is written into the manual
instead, in an @code{@@example} block with a line saying what it is.  A
diagram that silently disappeared from a manual would be worse than one
a reader has to copy.


@c %end of fragment

@c %start of fragment

@subsection Overview
@itemize 
@item
@ref{dokgen_diagrams_*diagram-destination*,*diagram-destination*} — A parameter object.


@item
@ref{dokgen_diagrams_*mermaid-command*,*mermaid-command*} — A parameter object.


@item
@ref{dokgen_diagrams_diagram-blocks,diagram-blocks} — Return the documentation string split into prose and diagrams.


@item
@ref{dokgen_diagrams_diagram-stem,diagram-stem} — Return the name a diagram is written under, without an extension.


@item
@ref{dokgen_diagrams_diagram-stexi,diagram-stexi} — Return the stexi nodes that show the diagram @var{source}.


@item
@ref{dokgen_diagrams_DEFAULT_MERMAID_COMMAND,DEFAULT_MERMAID_COMMAND} — A variable.


@end itemize


@c %end of fragment

@c %start of fragment

@subsection Parameters

@c %start of fragment

@anchor{dokgen_diagrams_*diagram-destination*}
@defvr Parameter *diagram-destination*
Default value:

@verbatim 
"manual/api"
@end verbatim

@end defvr


@c %end of fragment

@c %start of fragment

@anchor{dokgen_diagrams_*mermaid-command*}
@defvr Parameter *mermaid-command*
Default value:

@verbatim 
""
@end verbatim

@end defvr


@c %end of fragment

@c %end of fragment

@c %start of fragment

@subsection Procedures

@c %start of fragment

@anchor{dokgen_diagrams_diagram-blocks}
@deffn Procedure diagram-blocks docstring
Return the documentation string split into prose and diagrams.

@strong{docstring} (string): The documentation of a module or of one of
its objects.

@strong{Return value} (list of pairs): Every pair is either @code{(text
. STRING)} or @code{(diagram .  STRING)}, in the order they are written.
A fence that is never closed stays prose, because a docstring with a
typo in it should still reach the reader, and so does one written inside
a Texinfo block that quotes it.

@end deffn


@c %end of fragment

@c %start of fragment

@anchor{dokgen_diagrams_diagram-stem}
@deffn Procedure diagram-stem owner source
Return the name a diagram is written under, without an extension.

@strong{owner} (string): What holds the diagram: a procedure's name, or
a module's name.

@strong{source} (string): The diagram, as mermaid.

@strong{Return value} (string): The owner, with every character a shell
or a URL would have to escape replaced by a dash, and a digest of the
diagram.

@end deffn


@c %end of fragment

@c %start of fragment

@anchor{dokgen_diagrams_diagram-stexi}
@deffn Procedure diagram-stexi source owner
Return the stexi nodes that show the diagram @var{source}.

@strong{source} (string): The diagram, as mermaid.

@strong{owner} (string): What holds the diagram; see
@code{diagram-stem}.

@strong{Return value} (list of stexi): One node holding the image, in a
paragraph of its own because Texinfo writes an image inline where it
stands, or two nodes holding the diagram's source and a line that says
what it is when no image could be made.

@end deffn


@c %end of fragment

@c %end of fragment

@c %start of fragment

@subsection Variables

@c %start of fragment

@anchor{dokgen_diagrams_DEFAULT_MERMAID_COMMAND}
@defvr Variable DEFAULT_MERMAID_COMMAND
@verbatim 
"mmdc --input %i --output %o.png --scale 2 --backgroundColor transparent"
@end verbatim

@end defvr


@c %end of fragment

