@node dokgen_exceptions
@section (dokgen exceptions)

@c %start of fragment

This module defines the exceptions raised by the @command{dokgen}
program.

The exception type @code{&residual-export-exception} is raised when a
module exports a name that is not bound to any object.  This can occur,
for example, when a developer removes a procedure, variable, etc., from
a module but forgets to remove its name from the export list.

Its constructor, its predicate and its three field readers are defined
by @code{define-exception-type}, which gives them no documentation
strings; each one is given its own below, so that a name this module
exports is a name the manual can document.


@c %end of fragment

@c %start of fragment

@subsection Overview
@itemize 
@item
@ref{dokgen_exceptions_make-residual-export-exception,make-residual-export-exception} — Return a new @code{&residual-export-exception}.


@item
@ref{dokgen_exceptions_residual-export-exception-exported-residue,residual-export-exception-exported-residue} — Return the name that was exported but never bound.


@item
@ref{dokgen_exceptions_residual-export-exception-exporter-module,residual-export-exception-exporter-module} — Return the module that exports the residue, as a list of symbols.


@item
@ref{dokgen_exceptions_residual-export-exception-reason,residual-export-exception-reason} — Return the sentence that explains what went wrong.


@item
@ref{dokgen_exceptions_residual-export-exception?,residual-export-exception?} — Return @code{#true} when the given object is a residual export
exception.


@item
@ref{dokgen_exceptions_&residual-export-exception,&residual-export-exception} — A record type.


@end itemize


@c %end of fragment

@c %start of fragment

@subsection Procedures

@c %start of fragment

@anchor{dokgen_exceptions_make-residual-export-exception}
@deffn Procedure make-residual-export-exception a b c
Return a new @code{&residual-export-exception}.

@strong{reason} (string): What went wrong, in a sentence a reader can
act on.

@strong{exported-residue} (symbol): The name that was exported but never
bound.

@strong{exporter-module} (list of symbols): The module that exports it,
for example: @code{'(mylib amodule)}.

@end deffn


@c %end of fragment

@c %start of fragment

@anchor{dokgen_exceptions_residual-export-exception-exported-residue}
@deffn Procedure residual-export-exception-exported-residue obj
Return the name that was exported but never bound.

@end deffn


@c %end of fragment

@c %start of fragment

@anchor{dokgen_exceptions_residual-export-exception-exporter-module}
@deffn Procedure residual-export-exception-exporter-module obj
Return the module that exports the residue, as a list of symbols.

@end deffn


@c %end of fragment

@c %start of fragment

@anchor{dokgen_exceptions_residual-export-exception-reason}
@deffn Procedure residual-export-exception-reason obj
Return the sentence that explains what went wrong.

@end deffn


@c %end of fragment

@c %start of fragment

@anchor{dokgen_exceptions_residual-export-exception?}
@deffn Procedure residual-export-exception? obj
Return @code{#true} when the given object is a residual export
