@node dokgen_stats
@section (dokgen stats)

@c %start of fragment

This module measures a tree: how much of it is code, how much of that
code branches, who wrote it, and which files cost the most to keep.

What it reports is a small set of numbers a reader can reproduce.  The
lines of code, of comment and the bytes come from the files themselves;
the decision points are the branching forms a reader can find with a
search; the authors and the churn come from the repository's own
history.  Nothing here guesses, and nothing here grades: a file with
many decision points is a file that branches often, not a file that is
badly written.

@example 
(analyze-source "(display x)\n")
 => ((blank . 0) (comment . 0) (code . 1) (decisions . 0))
@end example

The parsers are separate from the calls that feed them, so the suite
that checks a log can hand over a log written by hand instead of
building a repository.


@c %end of fragment

@c %start of fragment

@subsection Overview
@itemize 
@item
@ref{dokgen_stats_analyze-file,analyze-file} — Return what the file at @var{path} is made of.


@item
@ref{dokgen_stats_analyze-source,analyze-source} — Return what @var{text} is made of.


@item
@ref{dokgen_stats_git-log,git-log} — Return the history of @var{directory} as git prints it, or
@code{#false}.


@item
@ref{dokgen_stats_git-stats,git-stats} — Return the numbers of the history of @var{directory}, or @code{#false}.


@item
@ref{dokgen_stats_parse-git-log,parse-git-log} — Return the history in @var{text} as the numbers a report needs.


@item
@ref{dokgen_stats_project-stats,project-stats} — Return the totals of @var{files} and the files in the order to show
them.


@end itemize


@c %end of fragment

@c %start of fragment

@subsection Procedures

@c %start of fragment

@anchor{dokgen_stats_analyze-file}
@deffn Procedure analyze-file path
Return what the file at @var{path} is made of.

@strong{path} (string): A path to a file of Scheme source.

@strong{Return value} (alist): Its name, the counts of
@code{analyze-source} and its size in bytes.

@end deffn


@c %end of fragment

@c %start of fragment

@anchor{dokgen_stats_analyze-source}
@deffn Procedure analyze-source text
Return what @var{text} is made of.

@strong{text} (string): Scheme source.

@strong{Return value} (alist): Lines of code, of comment and of nothing,
and the decision points the code holds; see @code{count-lines}.

@end deffn


@c %end of fragment

@c %start of fragment

@anchor{dokgen_stats_git-log}
@deffn Procedure git-log directory
Return the history of @var{directory} as git prints it, or
@code{#false}.

@strong{directory} (string): A path inside a repository; git finds the
repository above it.

@strong{Return value} (string or @code{#false}): What @command{git log}
prints for the commits that touch the tree, one line per commit and one
per file it touched, or @code{#false} when git could not read one.  It
is run without a shell, so a directory is a path and not something a
shell could read.

@end deffn


@c %end of fragment

@c %start of fragment

@anchor{dokgen_stats_git-stats}
@deffn Procedure git-stats directory
Return the numbers of the history of @var{directory}, or @code{#false}.

@strong{directory} (string): A path inside a repository.

@strong{Return value} (alist or @code{#false}): What
@code{parse-git-log} returns, or @code{#false} when the tree has no
history git can read.

@end deffn


@c %end of fragment

@c %start of fragment

@anchor{dokgen_stats_parse-git-log}
@deffn Procedure parse-git-log text
Return the history in @var{text} as the numbers a report needs.

@strong{text} (string): The output @code{git-log} returns.

@strong{Return value} (alist or @code{#false}): The commits, the newest
of them, the oldest and the newest dates, and what each author and each
file cost, largest first.  @code{#false} when there is no history in
@var{text}.

@end deffn


@c %end of fragment

@c %start of fragment

@anchor{dokgen_stats_project-stats}
@deffn Procedure project-stats files
Return the totals of @var{files} and the files in the order to show
them.

@strong{files} (list of alists): What @code{analyze-file} returns for
each file of the project.

@strong{Return value} (alist): @code{files}, largest first and then by
name, and the totals of the lines, the decision points and the bytes.

@end deffn


@c %end of fragment

@c %end of fragment

@c %end of fragment

@c %start of fragment

@node dokgen_templates_stexi
@section (dokgen templates stexi)

@c %start of fragment

This module defines procedures that structure @ref{dokgen_data,API data}
as @emph{stexi} (symbolic texinfo), which can later be translated into
Texinfo and integrated with the rest of the Texinfo documentation of a
given software project.


@c %end of fragment

@c %start of fragment

@subsection Overview
@itemize 
@item
@ref{dokgen_templates_stexi_api-binding,api-binding} — Return the API binding name-value as an stexi fragment.


@item
@ref{dokgen_templates_stexi_api-chapter,api-chapter} — Return a library API as an stexi chapter.


@item
@ref{dokgen_templates_stexi_module-description,module-description} — Return the module's commentary or description as stexi.


@item
@ref{dokgen_templates_stexi_module-overview,module-overview} — Return the module's exported objects as a list a reader can skim.


@item
@ref{dokgen_templates_stexi_module-section,module-section} — Return the module documentation as an stexi section.


@item
@ref{dokgen_templates_stexi_procedure-parameters,procedure-parameters} — Return the parameters of the given procedure as a string.


@item
@ref{dokgen_templates_stexi_stats-chapter,stats-chapter} — Return the statistics of a project as an stexi chapter.


@end itemize


@c %end of fragment

@c %start of fragment

@subsection Procedures

@c %start of fragment

@anchor{dokgen_templates_stexi_api-binding}
@deffn Procedure api-binding name value module-name
Return the API binding name-value as an stexi fragment.

@strong{name} (symbol): The name of the binding.  For example, the name
of a variable, the name of a procedure, etc.

@strong{value} (anything): Any kind of object.  For example, a string, a
list, a procedure, a record, etc.

@strong{module-name} (list of symbols): The name of the module where the
binding is defined.  For example: @code{'(mylib amodule)}.

@strong{Return value} (stexi): An stexi fragment that documents the
@var{value}.

@end deffn


@c %end of fragment

@c %start of fragment

@anchor{dokgen_templates_stexi_api-chapter}
@deffn Procedure api-chapter module-names sections
Return a library API as an stexi chapter.

@strong{module-names} (list of lists of symbols): The modules the
chapter documents, in the order they are documented.

@strong{sections} (list of stexi): A list where every item is an stexi
section.

@strong{Return value} (stexi): A chapter documenting a library's API,
opening with the list of its modules so that a reader who opened the
chapter to find one of them does not have to scroll for it.

@end deffn


@c %end of fragment

@c %start of fragment

@anchor{dokgen_templates_stexi_module-description}
@deffn Procedure module-description module-name
Return the module's commentary or description as stexi.

@strong{module-name} (list of symbols): For example: @code{'(mylib
amodule)}.

@strong{Return value} (stexi): An stexi fragment.

@end deffn


@c %end of fragment

@c %start of fragment

@anchor{dokgen_templates_stexi_module-overview}
@deffn Procedure module-overview objects module-name
Return the module's exported objects as a list a reader can skim.

@strong{objects} (alist): The API objects grouped by kind, as
@code{group-api-objects} returns them.

@strong{module-name} (list of symbols): The module they belong to, so
that every name links to its own definition.

@strong{Return value} (stexi): An @code{@@itemize} of the names with the
sentence that documents each, which is what a reader looking for one of
them scans first.

@end deffn


@c %end of fragment

@c %start of fragment

@anchor{dokgen_templates_stexi_module-section}
@deffn Procedure module-section module-name
Return the module documentation as an stexi section.

@strong{module-name} (list of symbols): For example: @code{'(mylib
amodule)}.

@strong{Return value} (stexi): A section documenting a module's API.

@end deffn


@c %end of fragment

@c %start of fragment

@anchor{dokgen_templates_stexi_procedure-parameters}
@deffn Procedure procedure-parameters proc
Return the parameters of the given procedure as a string.

@strong{proc} (procedure): A procedure object.

@strong{Return value} (string): A string listing the names of all the
required, optional, keyword, and rest of parameters of the procedure.
Default values for optional and keyword parameters are not included.

@end deffn


@c %end of fragment

@c %start of fragment

@anchor{dokgen_templates_stexi_stats-chapter}
@deffn Procedure stats-chapter statistics
Return the statistics of a project as an stexi chapter.

@strong{statistics} (alist): What @code{(dokgen commands) stats}
measured and counted: @code{totals} from @code{(dokgen stats)
project-stats}, the @code{coverage} of the exported names, the number of
@code{modules}, and @code{git}, the history or @code{#false} when the
tree has none.

@strong{Return value} (stexi): A chapter describing the tree: its size,
where its code sits, how much of its API is documented, who wrote it and
what churns.

@end deffn


@c %end of fragment

@c %end of fragment

@c %end of fragment

@c %start of fragment

@node dokgen_utils
@section (dokgen utils)

@c %start of fragment

This module defines helper procedures that didn't quite fit anywhere
else.  They normalize the indentation of documentation strings before
they are rendered.  The constant @code{DEFAULT_SPACE_INDENT_SIZE} is the
number of spaces that replace a tab when no other size is given; its
value is 2.


@c %end of fragment

@c %start of fragment

@subsection Overview
@itemize 
@item
@ref{dokgen_utils_min-indent,min-indent} — Return the shorter number of spaces used for indentation in the given


@item
@ref{dokgen_utils_tabs->spaces,tabs->spaces} — Convert tabs to spaces in the given string.


@item
@ref{dokgen_utils_trim,trim} — Trim off the given number of spaces at the beginning of the string.


@item
@ref{dokgen_utils_unindent,unindent} — Remove unwanted indentation from the given documentation string.


@item
@ref{dokgen_utils_DEFAULT_SPACE_INDENT_SIZE,DEFAULT_SPACE_INDENT_SIZE} — A variable.


@end itemize


@c %end of fragment

@c %start of fragment

@subsection Procedures

@c %start of fragment

@anchor{dokgen_utils_min-indent}
@deffn Procedure min-indent string
Return the shorter number of spaces used for indentation in the given
string.

This procedure assumes indentation is space-based, not tab-based.

@strong{string} (string): The text to inspect.

@strong{Return value} (integer): The number of spaces representing the
shorter indentation.

@end deffn


@c %end of fragment

@c %start of fragment

@anchor{dokgen_utils_tabs->spaces}
@deffn Procedure tabs->spaces string OPT: tabsize
Convert tabs to spaces in the given string.

@strong{string} (string): The original text.

@strong{tabsize} (integer): Optional.  The number of spaces that will
replace a single tab.  If not provided, @var{DEFAULT_SPACE_INDENT_SIZE}
is used.

@strong{Return value} (string): A new string where all tabs are replaced
by spaces.

@end deffn


@c %end of fragment

@c %start of fragment

@anchor{dokgen_utils_trim}
@deffn Procedure trim string spaces
Trim off the given number of spaces at the beginning of the string.

@strong{string} (string): The original text.

@strong{spaces} (integer): The number of spaces to trim off.

@strong{Return value} (string): A new string with the exact number of
spaces removed, if they exist.  Otherwise, the original string is
returned.

@end deffn


@c %end of fragment

@c %start of fragment

@anchor{dokgen_utils_unindent}
@deffn Procedure unindent docstring
Remove unwanted indentation from the given documentation string.

'Unwanted' indentation is what results, for example, from aligning
documentation lines to the first line of the documentation string so
that they look aesthetic in the source code.

@strong{docstring} (string): A string that documents a procedure or any
other object.

@strong{Return value} (string): A new string with the undesired
indentation removed.

@end deffn


@c %end of fragment

@c %end of fragment

@c %start of fragment

@subsection Variables

@c %start of fragment

@anchor{dokgen_utils_DEFAULT_SPACE_INDENT_SIZE}
@defvr Variable DEFAULT_SPACE_INDENT_SIZE
@verbatim 
2
@end verbatim

@end defvr


@c %end of fragment

@c %end of fragment

@c %end of fragment

@c %start of fragment

@node dokgen_writer
@section (dokgen writer)

@c %start of fragment

Procedures for writing data to disk.


@c %end of fragment

@c %start of fragment

@subsection Overview
@itemize 
@item
@ref{dokgen_writer_save,save} — Write @var{text} to the file in @var{path}.


@end itemize


@c %end of fragment

@c %start of fragment

@subsection Procedures

@c %start of fragment

@anchor{dokgen_writer_save}
@deffn Procedure save text path
Write @var{text} to the file in @var{path}.

@strong{text} (string): Arbitrary text.

@strong{path} (string): Absolute or relative path to the file the text
will be written to.

@strong{Result}: If the file doesn't exist, it will be created and the
text will be saved to it.  If the file exists, its contents will be
overwritten.

@end deffn


@c %end of fragment

